  nonce: ba8f  # ba8f
  message: "Pass 18 DDDDDDD root-cause analysis: traced cli.py:3866-3886 + io_boundary.py:1249 (total_io_edges=tagged_count). The 7859→6432 inversion isn't a single-metric value being filtered — it's two DIFFERENT METRICS reported under the same field name 'total_io_edges'. (1) JSON default with exclude_tests=True falls into cli.py:3870's filtered_total = sum(len(e.chains) for e in filtered_entries.values()) which counts production-filtered chains INCLUDING the external_potential bucket: 7016 ep + 843 non-ep = 7859. (2) JSON --include-tests falls into cli.py:3882's else branch which uses bmap.to_dict() and that surfaces bmap.total_io_edges = tagged_count from io_boundary.py:1249 — the count of boundary-tagged edges BEFORE external_potential is added: 6432. Additional bug: in the --include-tests JSON response, the boundaries.chains lists SUM to 25128 (sub-totals: ep=18696, fs_read=1593, fs_write=4395, env_read=152, subprocess=152, logging=125, others ≤10) but total_io_edges field reports 6432 — the summary value disagrees with the contents of the same response object. Fix: pick ONE metric (probably sum-of-chains, since that's what the response contains) and use it consistently in both code paths."  # ba8f
